# Explainable Fraud Detection and Intelligent Alert Allocation Pipeline

## Project Description
This project identifies suspicious financial transactions using rule-based fraud detection and provides reasons for generating alerts.

## Objectives
- Identify unusual transactions.
- Explain why a transaction is flagged.
- Support future intelligent allocation of alerts to analysts.

## Technology Used
- Python
- GitHub

## Current Implementation
The current program uses simple rules to identify suspicious transactions based on transaction amount, device information, and location.

## Future Enhancements
- CSV and Excel data processing
- Machine learning using Naive Bayes
- Schema drift detection
- Explainable alerts
- Analyst allocation using backtracking
- Precision, recall, and fairness evaluation
